# Copy to .env.readonly and fill in the rm_readonly role's connection details.
# Consumed by `bun run twin:capture` and the release preflight — see
# docs/runbooks/v0-2-2-rollout.md §3/§4 for how to provision the role.
#
# This is a SEPARATE file from .env, and holds a SEPARATE, read-only role's
# credentials — never the application's writer DATABASE_URL. Discrete keys,
# not a pasted postgres:// URL: the script builds and URI-escapes the
# connection string itself, so a password containing `@ : / ? # [ ] %` or a
# space is safe here without restricting the alphabet you generate it from.
#
# All five keys below are required. sslmode is optional and defaults to
# "require" if omitted — the managed cluster this points at always needs TLS.
#
# THIS FILE IS THE CREDENTIAL SOURCE FOR THE WHOLE TWIN / ROLLOUT FAMILY:
#
#   bun run twin            standing twin on the pinned tunnel port
#   bun run twin:capture    dump the read-only replica
#   bun run twin:rehearse   unattended digital-twin rehearsal
#   the per-release preflight
#
# None of them reads the repo-root `.env`, deliberately. On a staging host that
# file is where the application's WRITER DATABASE_URL lives, and this family of
# commands is DEFINED by not needing it — reading it would make the twin tooling
# depend on the one file it exists to stay away from, and make "which credential
# did that run use?" a question with two possible answers.
#
# The five keys below are what the preflight and the capture read; they ignore
# anything else. One extra key belongs here:
#
#   OPENCODE_API_KEY  — the funded OpenCode Zen credential. Its home for these
#                       commands is THIS FILE (the process environment still
#                       overrides it, which is how CI and a one-off shell supply
#                       it; an env var is not a file and cannot be the writer
#                       credential by accident). scripts/lib/opencode-key.ts
#                       still documents repo-root .env as the home for the
#                       ordinary standing demo — that is a different command
#                       family and is unchanged.
#                       It is REQUIRED: the twin boots the production model on
#                       purpose and refuses to run keyless, because model choice
#                       materially changes swarm authorship
#                       (scripts/lib/swarm/inference.ts).
#
# Beyond those, keep this file narrow. Its point is to be the low-privilege
# credential you can hand to a staging host — anything stored alongside
# inherits that file's blast radius, and the runbook's whole backup path
# (docs/runbooks §5) is deliberately one read-only role against a replica.

host=
port=25060
username=rm_readonly
password=
database=defaultdb
# sslmode=require
